## Impact on existing clones

If you had a local clone of this repo from **before 2026-09-10**, your `main` no longer fast-forwards from `origin/main`. You must either:

1. **Re-clone (recommended):**
   ```
   cd .. && rm -rf PANELTEC-SAFETY-PORTAL
   git clone https://github.com/Paneltec/PANELTEC-SAFETY-PORTAL.git
   ```

2. **Hard-reset your existing clone to the new remote tip:**
   ```
   git fetch origin
   git checkout main
   git reset --hard origin/main
   ```
   **Warning:** any uncommitted local work will be lost.

3. **Rebase your feature branches onto the new `main`:**
   ```
   git fetch origin
   git checkout your-feature-branch
   git rebase --onto origin/main <old-main-SHA> your-feature-branch
   ```

## Follow-up: don't push APKs again

`.gitignore` now blocks `backend/static/downloads/*.apk`. Do not `-f`-add APK binaries. Deliver Android builds via EAS artefact hosting or a signed release URL — the FastAPI endpoint at `/api/mobile/downloads/android/latest.apk` reads from the working-tree copy (which stays on the server via CI / deploy pipeline), not from git.

